  {
   "id": "aezZrwKtMQsJ",
   "from": "Joran",
   "author": "439a20c9d67ff394",
   "date": "2012-06-24T14:51:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: Bug, feature or PBKAC?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "When you set the axis limits to c(0.1,1) data values that represents the &quot;bottom&quot; of each bar falls outside those limits. The default action of ggplot for data that is outside those limits is to drop them completely. In the case of bars, this means you don&#39;t really have a bar to draw anymore. Try passing oob = rescale_none within scale_y_continuous. (oob stands for Out Of Bounds, I believe)<div><br></div><div>The behavior when the limits are set to c(-0.1,1.0) seems perfectly correct and natural to me. Was there something you thought was wrong with that version?</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br><br>On Sunday, June 24, 2012 3:40:08 AM UTC-7, Juan Carlos Borrás wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Dear all,<div>As the subject says. Given the following code (based on a simple variable called x that you can load from the attached x.RData file):</div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\"><br></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">class(x)</span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><font color=\"#0000ff\">&gt; &quot;data.frame&quot;</font></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:blue\">x\r\n</span>&gt;  Preference Resilience\r\n&gt;1  Arhinmäki  0.9675527\r\n&gt;2    Biaudet  0.9956700\r\n&gt;3    Essayah  0.9999996\r\n&gt;4   Haavisto  1.0000000\r\n&gt;5   Lipponen  0.8925269\r\n&gt;6   Niinistö  1.0000000\r\n&gt;7      Soini  0.9362242\r\n&gt;8   Väyrynen  0.7513179\r\n<span style=\"color:blue\">class(x$Preference)\r\n</span>&gt;[1] &quot;factor&quot;\r\n<span style=\"color:blue\">levels(x$Preference)\r\n</span>&gt;[1] &quot;Niinistö&quot;  &quot;Haavisto&quot;  &quot;Essayah&quot;   &quot;Biaudet&quot;   &quot;Arhinmäki&quot; &quot;Soini&quot;     &quot;Lipponen&quot;  &quot;Väyrynen&quot; \r\n<span style=\"color:blue\">class(x$Resilience)\r\n</span>&gt;[1] &quot;numeric&quot;</pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><br></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\">## The following code only generates a figure for limits=c(x,y) where x&lt;=0.0</pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important\">\r\n</span></font><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- ggplot(x, aes(x=Preference, y=Resilience, fill=Preference))\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- p + geom_bar() + opts(legend.position=&#39;none&#39;)\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- p + scale_fill_manual(values=c(&#39;#00577dff&#39;,&#39;#61bf1aff&#39;,&#39;#f7931dff&#39;,&#39;#007ac9ff&#39;,&#39;#ed1b24ff&#39;,</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">&#39;#edd866ff&#39;,&#39;#cd0009ff&#39;,&#39;#1b9345ff&#39;))\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- p + coord_flip() \r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- p + scale_x_discrete(name=&quot;Voter&#39;s Choice (1st. round)&quot;)\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:blue\">p &lt;- p + scale_y_continuous(name=&quot;Voter&#39;s Continuation (2nd. round)&quot;, limits=c(0.0,1.0))\r\n</span><span>p\r\n</span><font color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2\"><font color=\"#0000ff\"># Try limits=c(0.1,1.0) and you get only the theme background,</font></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2\"><font color=\"#0000ff\"># try </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-size:10.4pt;line-height:1.2\">limits=c(-0.1,1.0) and you get the actual plot with uglier scale</span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-size:10.4pt;line-height:1.2\"><br></span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;line-height:1.2\"><font color=\"#0000ff\"># Using:</font></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px\"><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"># version.string R version 2.15.1 Patched (2012-06-23 r59614)\r\n# nickname       Roasted Marshmallows   </pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\"><br></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;outline:none;border-style:none;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:1.2\">#and ggplot2 source install with commit info: </pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"># commit 1df1e826901a4631f36761536daabfc3068c4ddc<br></span></font></pre></span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:16px;white-space:pre-wrap\"># Author: Winston Chang ...\r\n# Date:   Tue Jun 12 14:19:19 2012 -0500</span></font><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;line-height:1.2\">\r\n</span></pre><div style=\"fon